data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Dispatch d002 reply: greet, tested\\n\\n## Files created\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` — `greet(name)` returns `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (string concatenation, exactly as specified).\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` — `unittest` tests covering a normal name (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`). The test inserts `\u003crepo\u003e/src` into `sys.path` via `os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \\\"..\\\", \\\"src\\\")` so the import works when run from the repository root.\\n\\nNo other files were touched.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nCommand run from the repository root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\nOutput:\\n\\n    ..\\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n    OK\\n\\nExit code: **0**\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\n- Branch: `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n- Commit: `b85b02f` — \\\"Add greet function with unittest tests\\\" (creates `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`)\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-reply.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_9","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788418292,"id":"chatcmpl-72a09174c30b414fb81595e02a4d0a25","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

